## Agent Flow

This project has the agent-flow workflow kit installed.

Use `/agent-flow` for every task:

```text
/agent-flow <task>
```

When the user types `/agent-flow <task>`, run `agent-flow run "<task>"` from
the project root. When the user types `/agent-flow` with no task, run
`agent-flow status` from the project root; continue an active run with
`agent-flow continue` if present, otherwise ask for a task in the
`/agent-flow <task>` format.

The AI infers tier and phase depth. Small tasks collapse phases automatically; feature work expands them. The chain pauses once for spec/slice-plan review.

```text
/agent-flow          # resume the active run
/agent-flow status   # progress
/agent-flow abort    # cancel the active run (artifacts preserved)
```

Command mapping: `/agent-flow status` → `agent-flow status`, `/agent-flow abort` → `agent-flow abort`.
Treat `/agent-flow` as a skill trigger, not as a shell path.

### Natural-language steering
- "deepen this, treat as feature" → escalate
- "redo the spec" → re-enter spec
- "decline this PR comment politely" → comment-decline branch

### Artifacts

Run artifacts: `.agent-flow/runs/<run-id>/`. Resumable across sessions because the artifact files are the state machine.

### Memory / Lore

Lore in `.agent-flow/memory/lore/` is auto-indexed and cited at run start. The `design` phase prompt includes a "Relevant lore" block with Constraint/Directive excerpts of matched entries. Cite where they apply; do not fabricate.

CLI: `agent-flow lore list / search "<query>" / compact [--apply] / init <slug>`. Schema: frontmatter + `## Constraint` / `## Rejected` / `## Directive`.
